  "prefLabel": "Ins 209.01 Petitions",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Ins 209.01 Petitions.\n\n(a) Any person may request a declaratory ruling from the department on matters within its jurisdiction by filing an original and 4 copies of the petition, and the petition for declaratory ruling shall set forth the following information:\n\n(1) The exact ruling being requested, including any rule or statute implicated;\n\n(2) The statutory and factual basis for the ruling, including any supporting affidavits or memoranda of law; and\n\n(3) A statement as to how the language of the rule or statute applies to the circumstances of the petitioner's case.\n\n(b) Any petition for declaratory ruling which does not contain the information required in (a) above shall be inadequate.\n\nSource. (See Revision Note at chapter heading for Ins 200) #13073-A, eff 7-27-20",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/ins200.html"
